ok, already found it in the spoilers:




     * Non-cursed potions of extra or full healing, or blessed potions 
of healing.
     * Holy water, if non-chaotic and not polymorphed into an undead 
monster or a demon.
     * The spell "cure sickness" at 0% failure rate (not the spells of 
healing or extra healing, even though they have the same name as the 
potions...).
     * #invoking the Staff of Aesculapius, the Healer Quest Artifact; 
however, like any other artifact, you can only invoke it every so often 
(very roughly, every few hundred turns). Save it for an emergency.
     * If not in Gehennom, and if it's safe to pray (see the praying 
spoiler for details), prayer. (Of course, one will only rarely see 
Demogorgon outside of Gehennom--a bones level where someone had summoned 
Juiblex by human sacrifice, say.) This suggests that one goal might be 
to leave Gehennom as quickly as possible...

     * The spell "cure sickness" at anything other than 0% failure rate 
(duh).
     * A non-cursed, and preferably blessed, unicorn horn. If sickness 
is your only trouble, a blessed horn has a 77.3% chance of fixing it; an 
uncursed horn will fix it 64.6% of the time.
     * Eucalyptus leaves. Not recommended, since like any food, there's 
a chance they're rotten and eating them will knock you out, which would 
be Bad.


